WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:06.170
So let's continue our discussion of ways in
which Donald Trump may try to subvert or challenge

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:09.980
the will of the people in November of 2020
to get himself reelected.

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:11.570
Let's talk about Michigan.

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:15.290
Michigan has been a big target of Donald Trump's
ire.

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:17.650
Michigan has been looking at vote by mail.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:22.880
They decided they are going to be sending
absentee ballot applications to every voter.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:30.710
Now, I want to remember let's not forget that
Michigan is not sending an absentee ballot

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:31.869
to everyone.

00:00:31.869 --> 00:00:38.800
Michigan is sending an application for an
absentee ballot to anybody who wants one.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:43.829
Trump tried to argue on Twitter last week
that by sending a ballot to everybody, Michigan

00:00:43.829 --> 00:00:44.860
is doing something wrong.

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:48.309
Remember that Michigan is sending an application
to everybody.

00:00:48.309 --> 00:00:54.690
And in Michigan, the lieutenant governor,
Garland Gilchrist, the second said to MSNBC

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:59.870
that he believes Trump realizes he's likely
to lose Michigan in November.

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:06.060
And so he is kind of stirring up all of this
controversy over vote by mail in order to

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:10.150
create a pretext to challenge the results
in Michigan.

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:15.330
The lieutenant governor recently said in an
interview with MSNBC, quote, I think that

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:19.680
the president wants to set us up so that there
can be a conversation about the legitimacy

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:22.830
of an election that he is looking to lose.

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:24.570
That is a really unfortunate thing.

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:27.810
That's not how we do democracy here in the
United States.

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:32.070
And we need to be ready to respond to that
forcefully.

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:38.330
So you don't need to think too hard to realize
there is a very good chance Trump is going

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:45.340
to call election results into question in
2020 in the November 2020 election.

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:48.490
Trump won in 2016 and he still says it was
rigged.

00:01:48.490 --> 00:01:54.920
So understand, for three years, Donald Trump
has been attacking the trustworthiness of

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:56.320
an election that he won.

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:59.410
So, of course, he's going to challenge the
results.

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:00.710
If he loses in November.

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:03.370
Now, whether he'll get away with it, we'll
discuss in a moment.

00:02:03.370 --> 00:02:06.350
In terms of Michigan, Trump won Michigan.

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:07.740
It was really close.

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:12.460
Trump won Michigan by about 11000 votes over
Hillary Clinton.

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:17.740
That was zero point three percent in terms
of a margin of victory.

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:21.430
Right now, Trump is losing to Biden in Michigan.

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:27.080
In the last four polls, Trump is down by three,
four, seven and eight.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:34.319
OK, the way to prevent Trump from credibly
arguing that the Michigan results are bogus

00:02:34.319 --> 00:02:42.050
is to defeat him in a landslide, to defeat
Trump so overwhelmingly in Michigan that there

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:46.140
is no credible way for him to say it was rigged.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:49.830
Then 10000 votes, 15000 votes were the difference
maker.

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:52.530
They are going to bring out every trick they
can.

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:59.440
And Michigan is very likely to be a primary
target, which is why Donald Trump keeps talking

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:01.720
about Michigan all the time.

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:04.800
Now, it's also always personal for Donald
Trump.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:08.920
Part of Donald Trump's focus on Michigan is
that he's been feuding with Gretchen Whitmer,

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:14.260
who's been the Democratic Michigan governor
overseeing the Corona virus response.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:17.620
And this is a surefire way for Donald Trump
to attack you.

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:22.540
She has been standing her ground against Donald
Trump when it comes to Corona virus and policy.

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:26.650
Her polling is much better than Trump's in
terms of corona virus handling.

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:29.040
So that makes Trump absolutely furious.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:31.680
Now, let's talk about whether this will work.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:39.920
I've said before, if Trump loses, he will
likely claim it was rigged, but he will leave.

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:43.660
It's not likely to be what we would call a
peaceful transition of power.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:49.880
So when you look back at the Bush handoff
to Barack Obama, when you look at the Obama

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:55.900
handoff to Donald Trump, we had what we would
call a peaceful transition of power.

00:03:55.900 --> 00:04:00.489
The outgoing president inviting the incoming
president to a White House visit, even though

00:04:00.489 --> 00:04:03.070
these were hard fought political battles.

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:07.410
We checked every single box for what we call
a respectful, proper, peaceful transition

00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:08.410
of power.

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:13.070
I would expect Trump to continue being the
petulant child that he's proven himself to

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:18.229
be, refusing to welcome Joe Biden to the White
House, refusing to do these perfunctory things

00:04:18.229 --> 00:04:19.229
that outgoing.

00:04:19.229 --> 00:04:21.309
Presidents do, and quite frankly, I don't
care.

00:04:21.309 --> 00:04:22.930
I don't want to get ahead of myself.

00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:25.610
If Biden wins, if Biden wins.

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:28.930
The only thing that will matter is that Joe
Biden won.

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:33.229
Trump can do whatever he wants as long as
he leaves and we can get back to something

00:04:33.229 --> 00:04:34.229
more normal.

00:04:34.229 --> 00:04:37.190
Now, let me throw out one other thing I've
been thinking about.

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:43.080
If Donald Trump loses and claims that it was
rigged and still ends up leaving, it could

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:44.770
be a good thing for the country.

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:51.009
And what I mean by that is Donald Trump has
successfully ignored, flouted, not flaunted,

00:04:51.009 --> 00:04:58.520
flouted checks and balances, ignored separations
of power, emoluments, attacking the media,

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:00.289
accusing TV hosts of murder.

00:05:00.289 --> 00:05:03.229
Justice Department deciding, hey, we're not
going to prosecute someone.

00:05:03.229 --> 00:05:05.849
Michael Flynn, who's already pleaded guilty.

00:05:05.849 --> 00:05:11.760
It might actually be reassuring for the United
States to see Trump argue, I really won, I

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:17.629
really won, I really won and still be forced
out because it would reassure us that at least

00:05:17.629 --> 00:05:23.819
some of our institutions are still working,
seeing that an institution still works.

00:05:23.819 --> 00:05:26.710
Seeing that a check and balance still functions.

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:32.229
Seeing Trump try to say it was rigged but
still having to leave could be exactly the

00:05:32.229 --> 00:05:37.160
reassurance we need that we will start to
get back to something approximating a more

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:38.160
normal government.

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:39.160
It's a thought.

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:42.020
And in the end, all that matters is that he
does leave.

00:05:42.020 --> 00:06:07.599
That's all that really matters

00:06:07.599 --> 00:06:30.629
in

00:06:30.629 --> 00:06:55.089
the end.

